From: hull
Subject: [PATCH] vhost-device-gpio: take queues of up to 1024, as i2c does

qemu 10.0's vhost-user-gpio-pci offers its guest virtqueues of 1024 and
has no property to make them smaller, and Linux's virtio-gpio driver
takes the size offered; vhost-device-gpio refused anything over 256,
"vring 0 requested queue size 1024 out of range (1-256)", its start
failed, and qemu's teardown of the half-started device then aborted on
`i != mr->ioeventfd_nb' in memory_region_del_eventfd. vhost-device-i2c
already takes 1024.

--- a/vhost-device-gpio/src/vhu_gpio.rs
+++ b/vhost-device-gpio/src/vhu_gpio.rs
@@ -44,7 +44,7 @@ const VIRTIO_GPIO_STATUS_ERR: u8 = 0x1;
 /// Virtio GPIO Feature bits
 const VIRTIO_GPIO_F_IRQ: u16 = 0;
 
-const QUEUE_SIZE: usize = 256;
+const QUEUE_SIZE: usize = 1024;
 const NUM_QUEUES: usize = 2;
 
 /// Queues
